            "description": "Watch Jordan vs Argentina highlights and goals from World Cup 2026 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 28, 2026. On June 28, 2026, the global spotlight turned to a high-stakes World Cup fixture as Jordan prepared to test their mettle against the formidable Argentina . This clash of styles promised an intriguing narrative as the underdogs sought to upset the rhythm of the South American giants. Argentina Command the Opening Half Argentina established their dominance early, dictating the tempo through superior possession. The breakthrough arrived in the 19th minute when Giovani Lo Celso stepped up to a free kick. With a clinical left-footed strike, he found the top left corner to give the Albiceleste the lead. The pressure intensified, and after Lautaro Martínez hit the woodwork, a VAR review confirmed a penalty for a foul on Marcos Senesi . Martínez took responsibility from the spot in the 31st minute, calmly slotting the ball into the bottom left corner to double the advantage. Jordan’s Fightback and Messi’s Decisive Strike The second half saw a revitalized Jordan side refuse to back down. Their persistence paid off in the 55th minute when Ehsan Haddad delivered a pinpoint cross to Mousa Al Tamari , who unleashed a powerful shot into the top left corner. This goal shifted the momentum, prompting Argentina to introduce Lionel Messi from the bench in the 60th minute to restore order. Messi wasted little time in making his mark. In the 80th minute, he stood over a free kick and delivered a signature moment, firing a left-footed shot into the center of the goal to make it 3-1. Despite a late flurry of substitutions and yellow cards for Jordan defenders Yazan Al Arab and Mohammad Abu Zraiq , the South Americans remained composed to see out the victory and secure three vital points.",
